menu "SPI NAND Flash configuration"

    config NAND_FLASH_VERIFY_WRITE
        bool "Verify SPI NAND flash writes"
        default n
        help
            If this option is enabled, any time SPI NAND flash is written then the data will be read
            back and verified. This can catch hardware problems with SPI NAND flash, or flash which
            was not erased before verification.

    config NAND_FLASH_ENABLE_WL
        bool "Enable wear-leveling (FTL) support"
        default y
        help
            Enable the flash translation layer / wear leveling (currently Dhara:
            bad-block remapping, garbage collection). When enabled, the legacy API
            and the wear-leveling BDL use Dhara. The espressif/dhara component and
            src/dhara_glue.c are built in.

            When disabled, wear-leveling is compiled out (dhara_glue.c and the dhara
            dependency are not included). Legacy spi_nand_flash_init_device() and the
            wear-leveling BDL APIs return ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED. Raw flash access
            remains available via nand_flash_get_blockdev() when BDL is enabled, or
            via the internal nand_init_device() / nand_* APIs for a custom FTL.

            WARNING: Using SPI NAND flash without wear leveling is NOT recommended for
            general storage or filesystem use. Raw NAND requires erase-before-program,
            bad-block handling, and wear management. Disable this option only if you
            provide your own FTL or need raw access for diagnostics / bring-up.

            After changing this option, delete the project's dependencies.lock and run
            "idf.py fullclean reconfigure". Changing the Kconfig alone is not enough:
            a stale lock still pulls espressif/dhara into the build (you will still see
            "NOTE: [1/3] espressif/dhara" in the logs).

    config NAND_FLASH_ENABLE_BDL
        bool "Enable Block Device Layer (BDL) support"
        depends on IDF_INIT_VERSION >= "6.0"
        default n
        help
            Enable Block Device Layer (BDL) support for SPI NAND Flash. This provides:
            - Standard esp_blockdev_t interface for layered architecture
            - Flash Block Device Layer (raw NAND flash access)
            - Wear-Leveling Block Device Layer (logical sector access with wear leveling)
              when NAND_FLASH_ENABLE_WL is also enabled
            - Advanced layered API (spi_nand_flash_init_with_layers) when wear-leveling
              is enabled
            When disabled, only the legacy API is available.
            When enabled, the legacy spi_nand_flash_init_device() is not available (returns
            ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED). Use spi_nand_flash_init_with_layers() when wear-leveling
            is enabled, or nand_flash_get_blockdev() for raw flash access.

            Note: This option requires ESP-IDF >= 6.0 (esp_blockdev component).
            Enabling this on ESP-IDF < 6.0 will result in a build error.

    config NAND_ENABLE_STATS
        bool "Host test statistics enabled"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_LINUX
        default n
        help
            This option enables gathering host test statistics and SPI NAND flash wear levelling simulation.

endmenu
